# SS-07 - Market-data and backtest qualification
Workstream ID: SS-07
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/7
Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: M2
Dependencies: SS-03, SS-04, SS-14

## Purpose
Distinguish a functioning teaching simulation from a point-in-time qualified research system.

## Tasks
- [ ] Reconcile representative OHLCV against permitted independent sources.
- [ ] Qualify differing adjusted inputs seen across separate live TCS requests;
  investigate provider precision/revisions and boundary sensitivity without silent rounding.
- [ ] Qualify exchange holidays, special sessions, suspensions, circuits and missing bars.
- [ ] Implement nominal-share corporate actions, dividends, bonuses/rights and delistings.
- [ ] Add complete configurable Indian fee/tax schedules and liquidity/circuit constraints.
- [ ] Define shared evaluation windows, return definitions, benchmarks and sensitivity.
- [ ] Add walk-forward/holdout methodology and survivorship/data-snooping disclosures.

## Acceptance criteria
- Point-in-time availability is not inferred from adjusted-history prefix invariance.
- Every quality gap is visible and unsupported experiments fail explicitly.

## Completion evidence
- Not started. M1 validates shape/causality, not independent market truth.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-11: Registered explicit research-quality gates.
- 2026-11-11: Separate TCS requests produced differing body-engulfing results.
  A same-process pair matched all 492 BSE bars/targets, but three fresh-process
  BSE requests differed in 203-210 bars by up to about INR 0.001 in adjusted OHLC.
  Tiny boundary crossings changed 15-22 target states. Exact comparisons follow
  the documented variant; no prices were rounded or replaced to hide the issue.
  Provider-side origin/precision remains unqualified. Preserve inputs for comparisons.
